1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,647
The conditions that cause a production
incident —

2
00:00:05,647 --> 00:00:07,499
a node failure,
a bad deploy,

3
00:00:07,499 --> 00:00:10,464
memory exhaustion —
are the same conditions that kill the

4
00:00:10,464 --> 00:00:12,078
agent responding to it.

5
00:00:12,078 --> 00:00:16,143
And an agent that holds its state in
memory doesn't degrade gracefully.

6
00:00:16,143 --> 00:00:17,404
It stops.

7
00:00:17,404 --> 00:00:20,123
Then a human restarts the incident from
zero,

8
00:00:20,123 --> 00:00:23,112
with no idea which remediation actions
already ran.

9
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:29,212
Continuum is an incident-response agent
whose memory lives in CockroachDB instead

10
00:00:29,212 --> 00:00:30,803
of in the process.

11
00:00:30,803 --> 00:00:34,519
It runs on AWS Lambda with no provisioned
concurrency,

12
00:00:34,519 --> 00:00:37,005
so every invocation starts cold.

13
00:00:37,005 --> 00:00:39,476
Which means the process is allowed to die.

14
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,595
Five agents,
one write path.

15
00:00:42,595 --> 00:00:46,352
Before any reasoning,
the orchestrator's first action is always

16
00:00:46,352 --> 00:00:48,798
a recovery read against CockroachDB.

17
00:00:48,798 --> 00:00:52,404
If an incident is already open,
it picks up from the durable state —

18
00:00:52,404 --> 00:00:53,916
never from scratch.

19
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:56,423
An alert fires.

20
00:00:56,423 --> 00:00:58,104
Bedrock embeds it.

21
00:00:58,104 --> 00:01:01,704
CockroachDB's vector index finds the
closest past incident,

22
00:01:01,704 --> 00:01:04,075
and Claude proposes the next step.

23
00:01:04,075 --> 00:01:07,356
That step is committed as executing —
before it runs.

24
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,527
Now watch.

25
00:01:09,527 --> 00:01:11,611
The process is killed mid-step.

26
00:01:11,611 --> 00:01:13,299
No graceful shutdown.

27
00:01:13,299 --> 00:01:14,602
No checkpoint.

28
00:01:14,602 --> 00:01:16,344
Nothing gets a chance to clean up.

29
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,162
The process is gone.

30
00:01:23,162 --> 00:01:25,859
The step is still there —
sitting in executing,

31
00:01:25,859 --> 00:01:27,919
with nothing alive that owns it.

32
00:01:27,919 --> 00:01:31,212
That row is the agent's memory,
and it outlived the agent.

33
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,269
A cold Lambda invocation.

34
00:01:37,269 --> 00:01:40,682
It reads CockroachDB first,
finds the interrupted step,

35
00:01:40,682 --> 00:01:42,763
and re-runs that exact step.

36
00:01:42,763 --> 00:01:44,390
Not from scratch.

37
00:01:44,390 --> 00:01:45,648
Not skipped.

38
00:01:45,648 --> 00:01:46,816
Not duplicated.

39
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,794
That isn't one lucky take.

40
00:01:50,794 --> 00:01:52,955
Fifty interrupted incidents.

41
00:01:52,955 --> 00:01:54,782
Fifty clean resumes.

42
00:01:54,782 --> 00:01:57,537
Zero duplicated actions,
zero lost steps —

43
00:01:57,537 --> 00:02:00,488
counted from the durable rows,
not from a log.

44
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:03,897
And it isn't only our own kill switch.

45
00:02:03,897 --> 00:02:06,884
Here,
AWS terminates the function itself,

46
00:02:06,884 --> 00:02:10,206
mid-step,
with no signal the process can catch.

47
00:02:10,206 --> 00:02:12,820
All fifteen recovered,
exactly once.

48
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,911
The memory layer scales with it.

49
00:02:15,911 --> 00:02:18,588
From one hundred incidents to ten
thousand,

50
00:02:18,588 --> 00:02:22,829
CockroachDB's vector index stays flat
while a full scan climbs away from it —

51
00:02:22,829 --> 00:02:25,000
six times faster at the top end.

52
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:31,077
The same memory is queryable live,
through CockroachDB's managed MCP server —

53
00:02:31,077 --> 00:02:34,392
read-only,
called by the application itself.

54
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,788
Type-checked,
linted and gated in CI,

55
00:02:37,788 --> 00:02:42,621
with the recovery contract pinned by tests
that hard-kill a real process on every

56
00:02:42,621 --> 00:02:43,576
push.

57
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,751
Agents will keep dying mid-task.

58
00:02:46,751 --> 00:02:50,088
Continuum is the one that picks up exactly
where it left off.
